# Stage 5 of Myth (TZX block 52 at $6C3F-$F03E): the annotations kit/mkgame.py writes src/stage5/*.asm from.
#
# The same engine as stage 1 (src/stage1/stage1.ann) assembled at other addresses, with the stage's own code: the
# flight through space and the duel with Dameron, the intro and the ending texts. Only 51 of stage 1's 310 routines
# recur byte for byte (tools/stage_names.py); they keep stage 1's names. The resident part $F03F-$FFFF
# (src/resident) is @equ here with stage 1's names.
#
# Variables outside the block: the screen, the play buffer, the resident part's routines and tables.
@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the screen's pixels
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen's attributes
@equ $5B00 PlayBuffer 4415 ; the play buffer $5B00-$6CFF (its tail $6C3F-$6CFF is in the block): 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear
@equ $F959 DigitGlyphs ; resident font from '0': 8 bytes a character, 7 rows drawn (RenderDigits)
@equ $F9B0 PlaySoundVector ; resident: JP to the AY effect starter (E = the effect number)
@equ $F9BF DecimalTable 10 ; resident: the words 10000, 1000, 100, 10, 1
@equ $F9FB Score 2 ; resident: the score's low four decimal digits, 0-9999 (AddScore)
@equ $F9FD ScoreHigh ; resident: the score's high two digits (ten thousands), 0-99 (AddScore)
@equ $FA00 BitReverse 256 ; resident: each byte with its bits reversed (the sprites drawn facing left)
@equ $FB00 ScreenLineTable 384 ; resident: the screen address of each of the 192 pixel lines (words)
@equ $FC90 KeyUp ; resident key reader: Z when UP is held (DEFINE KEYS / joystick patch its port and bit)
@equ $FC9F KeyDown ; resident key reader: Z when DOWN is held
@equ $FCAE KeyLeft ; resident key reader: Z when LEFT is held
@equ $FCBD KeyRight ; resident key reader: Z when RIGHT is held
@equ $FCCC KeyFire ; resident key reader: Z when FIRE is held
@equ $FCDB KeyHook ; resident: called before every key read (a RET, or the joystick / pause check DEFINE KEYS installs)
@equ $4134 EnergyBarScreen ; the HUD's energy bar: screen row 1, pixel line 1, column 20
@equ $6A00 TextGlyphRows 14 ; DrawTextLine's 7 (row, 0) pairs, inside the play buffer past the text pages
#
# The work space $FE01-$FEFD (InitStageState $96DD clears $FE08-$FE56 at the stage start). Stage 5 lays it out
# anew: the names are stage 1's where the job is the same (stage 1's address in the comment), new ones otherwise.
@equ $FE08 RandomSeed 2 ; NextSeed $9483: seed = seed x 5 + $15; $07CF at the stage start
@equ $FE0A RandomPointer 2 ; Random $9492: a pointer into the ROM whose bytes are the random numbers; reseeded from R at the stage start, $0D7A at the burst
@equ $FE0C DrawSavedSP 2 ; the real SP while Dameron's drawers walk SP over the line table
@equ $FE0E SavedSP 2 ; the real SP while ClearBuffer, DrawHero and DrawHeroFrame walk SP over their tables
@equ $FE2D ShotCursor ; FindShotSlot's round robin 0-15 over the hero's shots (stage 1's MissileCursor $FE27)
@equ $FE2F ItemsChanged ; stage 1's $FE4A: 1 after AddItem; only RedrawItemsIfChanged (no caller) reads it
@equ $FE30 LineCount ; the line counter of Dameron's drawers; 2 from InitStageState
@equ $FE32 InitOnly32 ; set to 1 by InitStageState, read by nothing (stage 1's InitOnly12)
@equ $FE35 ItemSelected ; stage 1's $FE17: the slot of CarriedItems the HUD shows (6, then 3 from StageSetUp)
@equ $FE36 ItemLast ; stage 1's $FE18: the last used slot of CarriedItems (6)
@equ $FE37 ItemFirst ; stage 1's $FE19: the first slot of CarriedItems (6)
@equ $FE38 MissileCursor ; AddMissileFrom's round robin over stage 1's missile records (kept, no caller)
@equ $FE3A FireLatch ; stage 1's $FE50: 1 armed (FIRE up), 0 after a press; the hero fires on the release
@equ $FE3B WorkByte ; scratch: StartBurst's shape bits (stage 1's WorkByte $FE14)
@equ $FE3D DameronArrived ; 1 once Dameron's approach reached line $14: his path and his missiles start
@equ $FE3E DameronX ; Dameron's X offset in pixels (0, never changed)
@equ $FE3F DameronY ; Dameron's top line from line 48 ($8E at the start, $14 after the approach, then his path)
@equ $FE40 DameronPathIndex ; the step in DameronPath ($FF at the start)
@equ $FE41 PendingHits ; 2 after a shot meets Dameron's mouth; DuelHit takes one a pass
@equ $FE42 FormChanged ; 1 after a form change: the drawers clear the old picture
@equ $FE43 DuelPhase ; $FF the intro, 0-3 Dameron's four forms, 4 won (the ending)
@equ $FE44 HitCounter ; the hits on the current form, 0-19 (20 change the form)
@equ $FE45 DuelTimer 2 ; the texts' timer: $044C at the start, - 2 a pass; $FFC3 from the duel's start and again after the win
@equ $FE47 TextShown ; 1 while the intro or the ending is on the screen (its rows flash)
@equ $FE48 BurstSmall ; stage 1's $FE3E: 1 a small burst (14 steps, doubled moves), 0 a big one
@equ $FE49 BurstTimer ; stage 1's $FE3D: the burst's step; $65 idle in stage 5, $FF just started, $64 StopBurst
@equ $FE4A TextPenShift ; DrawTextLine's pixel offset; also UpdateBurst's old particle column for EraseParticle
@equ $FE4B TextScratch ; a text line's third header byte (unused); also UpdateBurst's old particle row
@equ $FE4C GlyphWidthMask ; the current glyph's width mask (DrawTextGlyph)
@equ $FE4D PassCounter ; stage 1's $FE31: + 1 every pass, the animations' clock
@equ $FE4E InitOnly4E ; set to $10 by InitStageState, read by nothing (stage 1's InitOnly3A)
@equ $FE4F Energy ; stage 1's $FE3F: the hero's energy, 0 to $2E (full)
@equ $FE50 InitOnly50 ; set to $0D by InitStageState, read by nothing (stage 1's InitOnly40)
@equ $FE51 InitOnly51 ; set to 1 by InitStageState, read by nothing (stage 1's InitOnly41)
@equ $FE52 EnergyShown ; stage 1's $FE4D: the energy the HUD bar last drew
@equ $FE53 EnergyChange ; stage 1's $FE4E: the pending energy change ($80 and up drains, under $80 refills 2 a pass)
@equ $FE55 LivesFlash ; stage 1's $FE59: the lives boxes' flash step, 0-$10 ($10 idle)
@equ $FE56 GameOverTimer ; stage 1's $FE5B: never set in stage 5 (only GameOverStep and InitStageState's clear write it)
@equ $FE58 Lives ; stage 1's $FE61: lives left, from H at StageEntry
@inline $954E 5
@inline $957F 5
@isub $7934 LD BC,ScoreDigitsHigh

@module variables ; The stage's work space: the play buffer's tail, the shadow attributes, the HUD picture and the records over it
@about The block's first 5057 bytes ($6C3F-$77FF) are loaded with the stage and hold no code; they are byte for byte stage 1's ($6C3F-$6FFF and $76C0-$77FF zeros, the HUD picture and its colours at $7000-$76BF). $6C3F-$6CFF is the end of the play buffer ($5B00-$6CFF), which in stage 5 holds the intro's and the ending's text pages ($5B00-$61FF, $6200-$68FF, DrawIntroText $8DAF, DrawEndingText $8DDE). $6D00-$6FFF is the shadow of the screen's attributes. After StageSetUp $95E4 has dissolved the HUD onto the screen, the picture's space holds stage 5's records: Dameron's missiles (Missiles $7000, 8 x 6 bytes), the burst's particles (Particles $7100, 4 bytes each), the hero's shots (HeroShots $75E0, 16 x 8 bytes) and the digit picture (DigitBuffer $7640). The hero's record and the stars lie in the data area (HeroRecord $BA7E, Stars $BA86).
$6C3F s PlayBufferTail ; The last 193 bytes of the play buffer PlayBuffer $5B00-$6CFF
> ClearBuffer $96AC clears the play buffer to $6CFF with PUSH HL. In stage 5 the buffer holds the two text pages from PlayBuffer $5B00 to $68FF; this tail is not written or read by stage 5's code (no recording reads or writes $6C3F-$6CFF: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending). Zero as loaded.

$6D00 s ShadowAttributes ; The shadow of the screen's 768 attributes, the screen's layout
> StageSetUp $95E4 copies the HUD's colours into rows 0-5 and shows the whole shadow (ShowShadowAttributes $95B0); FillShadowAttributes $957F paints its boxes into it (HudBox1-4, the play area black). The rest of stage 5 colours the screen's attributes directly (Attributes $5800). s5-right: 896 bytes written ($6D00-$707F, with the missile records), 9350 reads at most. Zero as loaded.
$6DC0 PlayAttributes ; row 6: the first row of the play area (AttrShadowAddress $A000, kept from stage 1, no caller)

$7000 b HudPicture 32 ; The HUD as loaded: 48 lines of 32 bytes (linear, top first), then their colours at $7600 (6 rows of 32)
> The same 1728 bytes as stage 1's (src/res/stage1/picture-hud-32x48.png). DissolveHud $941B dissolves the 48 lines onto the screen's lines 0-47 and StageSetUp $95E4 copies the 192 colours into the shadow rows 0-5, once, at the stage's start. EndStage $78B5 saves the screen's lines 0-47 back here ($78CC copies the colours to HudColours $7600, CopyScreenToBlock $93F3 the lines to $7000) before the next block is loaded.
> In play the picture's space holds the records below. s5-right reads $6D00-$76BF (the dissolve and the records) and writes $7000-$707F and $75E0-$766F.
$7000 Missiles ; in play: Dameron's 8 missile records, 6 bytes each ($7000-$702F): +0 the column ($FF free), +1 the line, +2 the kind, +3/+4 the kind's own (ClearMissiles $7F10 fills 128 bytes with $FF)
$7030 MissilesEnd ; the stray ninth record FindFreeMissile $8C6C returns when all eight are busy; UpdateDameronMissiles $804A never reads it
$7100 Particles ; in play, at the duel's end: the burst's particles, 4 bytes each, $FF ends the list (StartBurst $91B9, UpdateBurst)
$74E0 ActorRecords ; stage 1's hero and actor records (14 x 18 bytes): only stage 1's routines left in the block with no caller (SpawnActor $9E9C, RunActorHandlers $9EB7, ClearActors $95BD) touch them
$75E0 HeroShots ; in play: the hero's 16 shot records, 8 bytes each ($75E0-$765F; +0 the column, $FF free, $FE ending; +1 the line; +2/+3 the screen address), ClearHeroShots $7F02
$7600 HudColours ; the HUD's 192 colours as loaded (rows 0-5); in play the hero's shot records 4-15 lie over them
$7610 HeroShots6 ; shot record 6; stage 1's AddMissileHigh $9F60 (kept, no caller) would write its missile records 8-15 here
$7640 DigitBuffer ; at the stage's start: the score's digit picture (RenderScore $7B14, RevealScore $967E), before ClearHeroShots fills $75E0-$765F with $FF; also the item count's digits (FormatItemCount, no caller from play)
$7660 HudColoursRest ; the colours of rows 3-5 past the shot records
@res stage5/picture-hud-32x48.bin

$76C0 s Unused76C0 ; 320 bytes ($76C0-$77FF) no stage-5 code reads or writes
> Stage 1's span table room ($76A0-$779B) and its unused tail. Stage 5 copies no spans: no operand of its code names $7680-$77FF (checked over the listing $7800-$A366), and no recording (s5-right, rzx-r5, ending) reads or writes any of it. Zero as loaded.


@module entry ; The stage's entry and set-up
@about Stage 5's block is entered at StageEntry $7800 by the resident stage loader with H = the lives. StageEntry sets up the stage (the work space $FE08-$FE56, the HUD, the duel's variables, the two text pages, the hero, the shot and missile tables, the stars) and falls into MainLoop. Stage 5 has no stage-completed exit: it returns to the loader only with E = 0 (no lives) or E = 1 (CAPS SHIFT + SPACE).
$7800 c StageEntry ; Start the stage: lives from H, variables, HUD, duel, texts, hero, stars, then the main loop
> Called by the resident stage loader with H = the lives left. Stores H in Lives ($FE58), then: InitStageState $96DD (clears $FE08-$FE56, the carried items from StartItems, the energy refill $2E in EnergyChange $FE53), StageSetUp $95E4 (the title, the HUD, the item strip rolled in, the score revealed), QuietPasses $965D (30 idle passes of 3 frames: the HUD's energy refill and lives flash run). Then FireLatch $FE3A = 0, Dameron's X DameronX $FE3E = 0 and Y DameronY $FE3F = $8E (below the play area), the path index DameronPathIndex $FE40 = $FF, the phase DuelPhase $FE43 = $FF (the intro text), the text timer DuelTimer $FE45 = $044C, the burst timer BurstTimer $FE49 = $65 (idle).
> Then DrawIntroText $8DAF and DrawEndingText $8DDE (the intro and the ending texts drawn into the play buffer at PlayBuffer $5B00 and $6200), ClearHeroShots, InitHero, ClearMissiles, InitStars, and falls into MainLoop.
> Witness: L1 3 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).

@module mainloop ; The main loop and its pass
@about MainLoop $7843 runs one step a pass with a HALT at its head, so stage 5 is frame-synced (stages 1-4 are not). s5-right: 3730 passes in 7940 frames, about 2.1 frames a pass. While a text page is up (the phase DuelPhase $FE43 is $FF before the duel, 4 after it) each pass adds TextPassDelay's $07D0 rounds; in form 3 and after the duel PaceLateForms adds $0320 or $07D0 rounds. The loop ends only on no lives (the hero's game-over count HeroGameOverCount $BA84 at 0: E = 0) or CAPS SHIFT + SPACE (E = 1); winning the duel leaves the ending text on screen and the loop running.
$7843 c MainLoop ; One pass: HALT, the hero, the shots, the stars, Dameron, the HUD, the missiles, the colours; CAPS SHIFT + SPACE quits
> The pass, in order: PassCounter $FE4D + 1, HALT, HeroControl, HeroFire, MoveShots, DrawShots, MoveStars, DameronFire, ApplyEnergyChange, DrawEnergyBar $9744 (the energy bar), LivesFlashStep, DrawStars, DuelStep (the texts or Dameron), UpdateBurst $9076 (the burst particles); then writes $02 and $FF to the screen bytes $4200-$4201 (pixel line 2, columns 0-1, in the HUD); TextPassDelay when the phase DuelPhase $FE43 is $FF (the intro) and again when it is 4 (won); DrawHero, UpdateDameronMissiles, ColourPlayArea (which ends in DuelHit).
> Then: the hero's game-over count HeroGameOverCount $BA84 at 0 ends the stage with E = 0 (GameOverExit). CAPS SHIFT (port $FEFE bit 0) and SPACE (port $7FFE bit 0) both held end it with E = 1 (QuitStage). SPACE alone does nothing: stage 5 has no item window (ItemWindow has no caller).
> Witness: L1 11697 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$78A1 MainLoopCaps ; CAPS SHIFT held: SPACE too quits
$78AE c GameOverExit ; No lives: end the stage with E = 0
> Reached from MainLoop when the hero's game-over count HeroGameOverCount $BA84 reaches 0 (HeroControl counts it down in state 3, after the last life). E = 0, then EndStage.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.
$78B3 c QuitStage ; CAPS SHIFT + SPACE: end the stage with E = 1
> Reached from MainLoop ($78A8); falls into EndStage with E = 1.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.
$78B5 c EndStage ; Leave the stage: hide the HUD boxes, save the HUD, fade, return E, H = lives, BC = the score's digits
> As in stage 1 at $789E, the same code with stage 5's addresses. E (pushed) is the outcome: 0 game over (GameOverExit), 1 quit (QuitStage). Clears the play buffer (ClearBuffer $96AC), hides the pieces boxes and the lives boxes with two inline attribute fills (FillAttributes $954E, EndPiecesBox and EndLivesBox), copies the HUD attributes (rows 0-5, $5800-$58BF) to HudColours $7600, clears the score (column 6, line 8, 6 x 8 bytes), the two middle HUD fields (column 14, 4 x 8; column 20, 6 x 8), the item strip (column 10, line 24, 12 x 16) and the pieces field (column 25, line 24, 6 x 16) with CopyToScreen from the cleared buffer PlayBuffer $5B00 (stride 0).
> Then saves the HUD bitmap (lines 0-47, 32 bytes wide) to HudPicture $7000 with CopyScreenToBlock $93F3 (over the missile records, no longer needed), fades the screen (FlashFadeScreen), clears it (ClearScreen $949F), waits 100 frames (WaitFrames $9546) and returns to the stage loader with E, BC = ScoreDigitsHigh (the six score digits) and H = Lives.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.
$78BC b EndPiecesBox 5 ; $954E's inline record: column 25, line 24, 6 x 2 cells, attribute 1 (the pieces boxes hidden)
> Read by FillAttributes $954E (@inline 5) after the CALL at $78B9: column, line, width and height in cells, attribute.
$78C1 c EndStageLives ; EndStage, continued: hide the lives boxes
> Part of EndStage, after the first inline record.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.
$78C4 b EndLivesBox 5 ; $954E's inline record: column 1, line 24, 6 x 2 cells, attribute 1 (the lives boxes hidden)
> Read by FillAttributes $954E after the CALL at EndStageLives $78C1, in EndPiecesBox's format.
$78C9 c EndStageSave ; EndStage, continued: save the HUD, clear its fields, fade, return
> Part of EndStage, after the second inline record.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.

@module render ; Drawing: the fades, the screen copies, the play area's colours
@about Stage 5 draws straight to the screen: the hero (DrawHero), its shots (DrawShots), the stars (DrawStar), Dameron's three parts (DrawDameronFace, DrawDameronDome, DrawDameronBack) and his missiles are copied to the screen with no mask, each picture carrying blank edges that wipe its trail. The play area's colours are one colour a pass (ColourPlayArea, from the cycle CycleColour $A021). The play buffer $5B00-$6CFF holds the two text pages.
$793C c FlashFadeScreen ; Fade every coloured ink up to white over 7 frames, then down to black over 7 frames
> As in stage 1 at $7925, the same code. Seven times (HALT each): every attribute whose ink is neither 0 nor 7 gets ink + 1. Then seven times (two HALTs each): every ink not 0 gets ink - 1. Inputs: none; changes the attributes $5800-$5AFF. Called by EndStage.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.
$793E FadeUpFrame
$7946 FadeUpCell
$7952 FadeUpNext
$795E FadeDownFrame
$7967 FadeDownCell
$796E FadeDownNext
$7979 c CopyToScreen ; Copy a block of bytes to the screen, line by line
> As in stage 1 at $79CC, the same code. Inputs: HL = the source, B = the screen column, C = the first pixel line, D = the width in bytes, E = the lines, A = the source's stride (added to HL after each line; 0 repeats one source line, used with the cleared buffer to clear a screen block). Patches the column into $7992 and the stride into $79A3, then for each line takes the line's address from ScreenLineTable and LDIRs D bytes. Destroys IX, BC, DE.
> Callers: EndStage, ShowScore, ShowItemCount, GameOverStep and RevealScore $967E (the score revealed at the start).
> Witness: L1 48 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$798C CopyToScreenLine

@module duel ; The duel with Dameron: the texts' timer, his four forms, his path, his missiles, the hits
@about Dameron is a 15-column head on the right, drawn in three parts every pass: the face (7 bytes wide at column (X + $78) / 8), the dome (4 wide at (X + $B0) / 8) and the back (4 wide at (X + $D0) / 8), 128 lines from line 48 + Y (the line table ScreenLinePlay $9805). X (DameronX $FE3E) stays 0 (DameronPath moves only Y), so the columns are 15, 22 and 26. Y (DameronY $FE3F) starts at $8E, climbs one line a pass to $14 (DameronApproachStep), then follows DameronPath (one line up or down a pass, 128 steps).
@about The phase DuelPhase $FE43: $FF the intro text (TextPassDelay, the timer DuelTimer $FE45 from $044C down by 2 a pass to $00A0: 470 passes), 0-3 Dameron's four forms, 4 won (the ending text). A hero shot on the hit line sets the pending hits PendingHits $FE41 = 2; DuelHit takes one a pass into the hit counter HitCounter $FE44; at 20 (10 shots) the phase steps, FormChanged $FE42 = 1 and NextDameronForm $A0C4 bursts the old form. Form 0 face DameronFace0 $A43A, form 1 face DameronFace1 $ABBA, form 2 a 5-byte face DameronFace2 $AF3A, form 3 no face (the dome from DameronDome3 $B1BA); won: the dome and the back cleared and the final burst (FinalBurstShape).
$79A9 c DuelHit ; Take one pending hit a pass: count it, step the form every 20, flash Dameron's cells blue; while a text is up flash it instead
> Reached by a JP from ColourPlayArea every pass. TextShown $FE47 = 1 (a text page on screen, set by ShowTexts $8C87): FlashTextRows and return. Else when the pending hits PendingHits $FE41 are 0: return. Else PendingHits $FE41 - 1 and the hit counter HitCounter $FE44 + 1; at $14 (20): HitCounter $FE44 = 0, the phase DuelPhase $FE43 + 1, FormChanged $FE42 = 1 and NextDameronForm $A0C4 (effect 0 and the bursts of the beaten form; the final burst at phase 4).
> Then (DuelHitFlash) the 15 x 16 cells from $58C0 + (Y AND $F8) x 4 + (X + $78) / 8 (Dameron's face and dome) get attribute 1 (blue on black) for this pass; ColourPlayArea recolours them on the next.
> A shot gives two hits (MoveShots sets PendingHits $FE41 to 2), so a form takes 10 shots and the duel 40. s5-right never hit Dameron ($79B7 never ran); rzx-r5 counted all 80 hits ($79B7 80 runs, 40 shots on the hit line) and won the duel.
> Witness: L1 11696 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$79DB DuelHitFlash ; Dameron's cells blue for one pass
$79FE DuelHitFlashRow ; 15 cells, then + $12 to the next row
$7A22 c FlashTextRows ; Flash the seven text rows' attributes red and magenta
> While a text page is shown (TextShown $FE47 = 1): FlashTextRow on the rows 8, 10, ..., 20 at column 16 ($5910, $5950, $5990, $59D0, $5A10, $5A50, $5A90), the rows CopyTextLine $8D89 copies the text lines to.
> Witness: L1 4440 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$7A4D c FlashTextRow ; Fill 12 attributes at HL with bright red ($42) on even passes, bright magenta ($43) on odd ones
> HL = the first attribute; the colour from PassCounter $FE4D bit 0. HL is left past the 12 cells.
> Witness: L1 31075 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$7A59 FlashTextRowFill

@module render
$7A72 c ColourPlayArea ; Colour the whole play area (rows 6-23, columns 2-29) with this pass's cycle colour, then DuelHit
> A = CycleColour $A021 (the colour cycle by PassCounter AND 7: bright yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, magenta, green, cyan, the bytes at CycleColours $A02F); fills 18 rows of 28 cells from $58C2, unrolled. Then JP DuelHit, which may paint Dameron's cells blue or flash the text over it. Every pass: the stars, the hero, the shots and Dameron all take the one colour.
> Witness: L1 11696 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$7A7D ColourPlayAreaRow

@module mainloop
$7ABB c PaceLateForms ; Pad the pass in Dameron's form 3 and after: wait $0320 rounds (phase 3) or $07D0 (phase 4)
> Reached by a JP from DuelStep ($8855) with A = the phase DuelPhase $FE43, 3 or more: form 3 (no face drawn) and the end cost less, so the pass is padded with a busy count of HL down to 0 (26 T-states a round): $07D0 when A is 4, else $0320. Returns to DuelStep's caller.
> Witness: L1 472 (ending, rzx-r5).
$7AC6 PaceLateFormsLoop
$7ACD c TextPassDelay ; Busy wait $07D0 rounds: the pass pacing while the intro or the ending text is up
> Called by MainLoop when the phase DuelPhase $FE43 is $FF (the intro) and when it is 4 (won). Counts HL from $07D0 to 0 (about 52 000 T-states, 0.75 frame). Destroys A, HL.
> Witness: L1 5537 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$7AD0 TextPassDelayLoop

@module duel
$7AD7 b FinalBurstShape 2 ; The final burst's shape: 12 rows of 16 bits, bits 7-14 set (a block 8 fragments wide, 12 high)
> Read by StartBurst $91B9 (IX = $7AD7, D = 12, E = 9, A = 1) from $A0E2, at phase 4 (Dameron beaten): each set bit (bit 7 of the first byte first) puts a burst fragment at column D + bit, row E + row. Every row is $01, $FE.
@res stage5/bitmaps-final-burst-2x12.bin
$7AEF b FinalBurstShapeTail 4 ; Two more rows of FinalBurstShape's pattern that no code reads
> StartBurst $91B9 reads 24 bytes (12 rows of 2); these 4 bytes ($01, $FE, $01, $FE) continue the pattern up to AddScore. No code reads them: no operand points into them, and StartBurst $91B9 stops after 24 bytes.

@module hud ; The energy, the lives, the score, the HUD and game over
@about The routines stage 5 keeps from stage 1's HUD. The score is six decimal digits in the resident Score and ScoreHigh; stage 5 never adds to it (AddScore has no caller) and never shows it after the start (ShowScore has no caller; RevealScore $967E reveals it once). The energy (Energy $FE4F, $2E full) moves 2 a pass towards the pending EnergyChange $FE53; when it would reach 0 a life is lost and the hero explodes (state 1 of the hero record HeroRecord $BA7E). The six lives boxes flash after each life lost (LivesFlashStep).
$7AF3 c AddScore ; Add BC points to the score
> As in stage 1 at $7B53, the same instructions. Score += BC; at 10000 or more, Score -= 10000 and ScoreHigh + 1 (wrapping from 99 to 0). Outputs none; A, BC, HL destroyed.
> No caller in stage 5's code: no CALL, JP or pointer to $7AF3 in the linear listing list-all.txt.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.
$7B14 c RenderScore ; Write the six score digits into ScoreDigits and draw them into the text buffer $7640
> As in stage 1 at $7B73, the same code. $94F0 writes Score as four digits at ScoreDigitsLow, ByteToDigits $9524 writes ScoreHigh as two at ScoreDigitsHigh, then RenderDigits draws the six characters into DigitBuffer $7640 with a stride of 6. Called once by StageSetUp $95E4 (the stage's set-up).
> Witness: L1 3 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$7B36 c HideLeadingZeros ; Colour the score's leading zeros blue on black (unseen) and the rest yellow
> As in stage 1 at $7B95, the same code. Builds six attributes at $6D00 ($06, yellow on black), sets $01 for each leading '0' of ScoreDigitsHigh on, and copies them to the HUD at $5826 (row 1, columns 6-11). Reached only from ShowScore.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.
$7B4A HideLeadingZerosNext
