@module hero ; The hero: its movement, its shots, its explosion, and the item strip kept from stage 1
@about The hero is a 3-byte, 24-line sprite (HeroFrames: 4 animation frames x 4 two-pixel shifts) copied to the screen from the record HeroRecord $BA7E: +0 X in pixels ($12-$66), +1 the screen line ($40-$96), +4 the state (0 flying, 1 exploding, 2 re-forming, 3 game over), +5 the explosion frame, +6 the game-over count ($5A). The keys move it 2 pixels a pass in state 0 (HeroControl). FIRE shoots on its release (HeroFire): the shot records at HeroShots $75E0 (16 x 8 bytes: +0 the column, $FF free, $FE ending; +1 the line; +2/+3 the screen address) fly one column a pass to column 29 (MoveShots, DrawShots).
@about The item strip, the item window and the item counts are stage 1's code left in the block: StageSetUp $95E4 rolls the strip in at the start (ScrollItemsLeft three times, FlashSelectedBox); nothing else of it runs.
$7BCB c ItemWindow ; SPACE: stop the game, flash the strip's frame, choose an item with LEFT and RIGHT, SPACE again to go on
> As in stage 1 at $7C27, the same code. Clears PassCounter, waits (cycling the frame colours, CycleWindowFrame) for SPACE's release (TestSpaceKey $93BE), then every 6 frames: DrawItemStrip and ShowItemCount; RIGHT (KeyRight $FCBD) scrolls to the previous slot (ScrollItemsRight), LEFT (KeyLeft $FCAE) to the next (ScrollItemsLeft); SPACE again: waits for its release, cycles the frame back to its first colour (the attribute $586A at 1) and falls into FlashSelectedBox.
> No caller in stage 5's code: no CALL, JP or pointer to $7BCB in list-all.txt other than its own loop ($7BD7); stage 5's main loop does not test SPACE alone.
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s5-right, rzx-r5, ending); known only from the code.
