@module texts ; The intro and ending texts: their font, the drawing into buffers and the copy to the screen
@about Stage 5 shows two texts of seven lines each, the intro ("HURTLING ACROSS THE VOID OF SPACE. PRAPARE TO CONFRONT THE EVIL ANGEL OF TIME.DAMERON.") before the duel and the ending ("WELL DONE. YOUR TASK IS COMPLETE. HISTORY IS RESTORED AND DAMERON IS BANISHED.") after it. Both are drawn once at the start (DrawIntroText, DrawEndingText) in a proportional font (TextFont) into seven 256-byte pages of the play buffer each ($5B00-$61FF and $6200-$68FF), a page holding one line of 12 bytes x 8 pixel lines; ShowTexts copies one set to screen rows 8-20, columns 16-27, while the duel timer DuelTimer $FE45 runs.
$8C87 c ShowTexts ; Copy the intro or the ending text to the screen, or clear it, by the duel's phase and timer
> Jumped to from $87EB and $87F3 (the main loop's timer step) after the duel timer DuelTimer $FE45 was counted down by 2. HL = the timer, A = the phase DuelPhase $FE43.
> Phase 4 (Dameron beaten): ShowEnding. Otherwise by the timer's high byte: 2, or 1 with a low byte other than 0, shows the intro (TextShowing TextShown $FE47 = 1, the seven intro pages $5B00-$61FF copied by CopyTextLine to the screen at $4800, $4840, $4880, $48C0, $5000, $5040, $5080: character rows 8, 10, ... 20, columns 16-27), then waits 1300 loops of DEC HL (about 31 000 T-states, under half a frame); exactly $0100 clears the text (ClearTextArea: TextShowing = 0, BlankTextLine copied to the same seven places); any other value returns at once.
> In s5-right the timer starts at $044C (set at $7826) and goes down by 2 a pass: the intro is copied on the 255 passes from $02FE to $0102, cleared once at $0100, and the duel starts at $00A0 ($87F6: phase 0, timer $FFC3).
> Output: none. Side effects: TextShowing TextShown $FE47, the screen's pixels in rows 8-20, columns 16-27.
> Witness: L1 5535 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$8CA1 ShowIntro ; the intro's seven pages to the screen
$8CE8 ShowIntroDelay ; 1300 x (DEC HL until 0)
$8CEF ShowEnding ; phase 4: the timer's high byte $FF or $FE returns; else the ending's pages $6200-$68FF, then the delay
$8D3D ShowEndingDelay
$8D44 ClearTextArea ; timer $0100: TextShowing = 0 and BlankTextLine over the seven text lines
$8D89 c CopyTextLine ; Copy one text page (8 lines of 12 bytes) from HL to the screen at DE + 16
> Input: HL = the page (12 bytes a pixel line, packed), DE = the screen address of the character row's first line. E + 16 (column 16); 8 lines, each 12 LDIs, then INC D (the next pixel line of the character row). Output: HL past the 96 bytes. Corrupts A, BC, DE.
> Called 7 times from each of ShowIntro, ShowEnding and ClearTextArea.
> Witness: L1 31101 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$8D8F CopyTextLineRow
$8DAF c DrawIntroText ; Draw the intro's seven lines into the pages $5B00-$61FF
> IY = IntroText; DrawTextLine for each page PlayBuffer $5B00, $5C00, ... $6100 (IY runs on from line to line). Called once at the stage start ($7831).
> Witness: L1 3 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$8DDE c DrawEndingText ; Draw the ending's seven lines into the pages $6200-$68FF
> IY = EndingText; DrawTextLine for each page $6200 ... $6800. Called once at the stage start ($7834), right after DrawIntroText: the ending waits in the play buffer's pages for the whole duel.
> Witness: L1 3 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$8E0D t IntroText ; The intro's seven lines: each 3 header bytes, the characters, 0
> Format of a line (DrawTextLine): byte 0 the start column in bytes (0-11) within the 12-byte line, byte 1 the start pixel offset (0-7), byte 2 a byte stored in TextScratch $FE4B and never used for the text, then ASCII characters (A-Z, space, `\` drawn as a full stop; digits would index past TextFont), then 0. All headers here are 0, 0, 0: every line starts at the left edge.
> The text, as printed (sic): HURTLING / ACROSS THE / VOID OF SPACE. / PRAPARE TO / CONFRONT THE / EVIL ANGEL OF / TIME.DAMERON. Read once by DrawIntroText through IY (DrawTextLine).
