@module duel
$A0C4 c NextDameronForm ; Dameron's next form: seven explosions round his head, or at phase 4 the burst
> Called by DuelHit ($79D8) after the 20th hit of a phase has stepped the phase DuelPhase $FE43. PlaySoundVector $F9B0 with E = 0. Phase 1: SpawnFormExplosions1, 2: SpawnFormExplosions2, 3: SpawnFormExplosions3; any other (4): StartBurst (JP) with D = 12, E = 9 (column 12, row 9), A = 1 (small: 14 steps), IX = FinalBurstShape $7AD7 (the head's 16 x 12 shape).
> Witness: L1 8 (ending, rzx-r5).
$A0E9 b UnusedRet2 1 ; A RET no code reaches
> After NextDameronForm's JP StartBurst; no CALL, JP or word in stage 5's block names $A0E9 (work/stage2/stage5/B-raw.py).
$A0EA c SpawnFormExplosions1 ; Seven explosions round Dameron's head for his second form (phase 1)
> The base: E = DameronX $FE3E / 8 + 14 (column), D = (DameronY $FE3F AND $F8) + $48 (line). Each explosion: FindFreeMissile $8C6C finds a free shot record (IX), then +0 = E + dx, +1 = D + dy, +2 = 4 (the kind: the explosion handler BurstMissile $819D), +4 = its start count (negative: the handler counts it up every second pass and shows nothing until it reaches 0, so the seven go off one after the other). (dx, dy, +4): (0, $10, $FF), (2, $18, $FC), (4, $20, $FA), (4, 8, $FE), (1, $18, $F6), (3, 8, $F9), (-1, $10, $F2).
> Each FindFreeMissile $8C6C is followed by RET Z, but FindFreeMissile $8C6C returns NZ both when it finds a record and when the eight are busy (then IX = MissilesEnd $7030, past the records): the RET Z is never taken.
> Witness: L1 2 (ending, rzx-r5).
$A1B2 c SpawnFormExplosions2 ; Seven explosions round Dameron's head for his third form (phase 2)
> As SpawnFormExplosions1 with the base E = DameronX / 8 + 12, D = (DameronY AND $F8) + 8 and (dx, dy, +4): (0, $10, $FF), (2, $18, $FC), (4, $20, $FA), (3, 8, $FE), (1, $18, $F6), (1, $28, $F9), (-1, $20, $F2).
> Witness: L1 2 (ending, rzx-r5).
$A27A c SpawnFormExplosions3 ; Seven explosions round Dameron's head for his fourth form (phase 3)
> As SpawnFormExplosions1 with the base E = DameronX / 8 + $13, D = DameronY AND $F8 and (dx, dy, +4): (0, 0, $FF), (2, $18, $FC), (1, 8, $FA), (-1, $28, $FE), (1, $18, $F6), (3, $18, $F9), (2, $10, $F2).
> Witness: L1 2 (ending, rzx-r5).

@module missiles
$A33E c CheckShotHitsHero ; Damage the hero by 9 when the shot IX meets him
> Called for every used shot record by UpdateMissile $8065 each pass. The hero's column = HeroRecord $BA7E / 8 must equal +0; d = HeroLine $BA7F - $20 - (+1) (his line less the shot's); a hit when -7 <= d <= 13: DamageHero $7EDA with C = 9 (EnergyChange $FE53 - 9). The shot is not freed.
> In s5-right the column matched 391 times, the line never: no shot hit the hero; ending: 32 hits (CheckShotHitsDamage $A361), 5 lives lost.
> Witness: L1 14710 (ending, rzx-r5, s5-right).
$A35E CheckShotHitsBelow ; d >= 0: a hit under 14
$A361 CheckShotHitsDamage

@module graphics ; The stage's pictures: GAME OVER, the stars, Dameron's head in its forms, the sprite bank, the item icons, the hero
@about Stage 5's data runs from GameOverPicture $A367 to $BE7B; the rest of the block ($BE7C-$F03E) is zeros but for one byte. Everything is plain 1-bit bitmaps, rows top first, bit 7 the left pixel, no mask, copied (not ORed) straight to the screen through the screen-line tables. Each file of src/res/stage5/ is one entry (bitmaps-NAME-WxH: frames of W bytes x H lines one after another). s5-right reads the stars, Dameron's form-0 face, dome and back, the sprite bank's frames 0-3 ($B3BA-$B479, the fireballs), two item icons, the energy-bar pattern and the hero's frames; rzx-r5 and ending (the duel won) also read face 1, face 2, dome 3, the curved shot's frames, the bolts and the bursts. Read in no recording: GameOverPicture, SpriteBankSpare, BitMasks, ItemIconSpare, UnusedWordTable and the zero runs.
$A367 b GameOverPicture 8 ; GAME OVER: 8 bytes x 8 lines (the last line blank)
> GameOverStep $7E9D copies it to column 12, line $1C of the item strip (CopyToScreen $7979, BC = $0C1C, DE = $0808) when GameOverTimer reaches $31. Nothing in stage 5 sets GameOverTimer, so it is never shown: not read in s5-right; known only from the code ($7EBD).
@res stage5/bitmaps-game-over-8x8.bin

$A3A7 s UnusedA3A7 ; 89 zero bytes no code reads (no operand names $A3A7-$A3FF; no recording reads any)

$A400 b StarSlow 3 ; The slow star: two frames of 3 bytes x 3 lines ($A400, $A409)
> DrawStar $869C draws a slow star (+2 = 0) with the frame at $A400 when its X AND 7 is 0, else StarSlow1 $A409 (the star is 4 pixels on, half a byte). Read in s5-right (21103 + 10077 runs of the copy).
$A409 StarSlow1 ; frame 1: the star 4 pixels to the right
@res stage5/bitmaps-star-slow-3x3.bin

$A412 b StarFast 4 ; The fast star: two frames of 4 bytes x 5 lines ($A412, $A426)
> DrawStar $869C draws a fast star (+2 = 1) with $A412 on even passes and StarFast1 $A426 on odd ones (PassCounter bit 0): a twinkle. Read in s5-right.
$A426 StarFast1 ; frame 1: the twinkle
@res stage5/bitmaps-star-fast-4x5.bin

$A43A b DameronFace0 7 ; Dameron's face, form 0: 7 bytes x 128 lines
> DrawDameronFace $8859 copies it (phase 0) at column (DameronX + $78) / 8, from line 48 + DameronY, with SP walking the line table; 128 lines, or $36 while DameronY >= $5A. Read in s5-right (3259 passes).
@res stage5/bitmaps-dameron-face0-7x128.bin

$A7BA b DameronDome 4 ; The middle of Dameron's head, forms 0-2: 4 bytes x 128 lines
> DrawDameronDome $894D, at column (DameronX + $B0) / 8. Read in s5-right.
@res stage5/bitmaps-dameron-dome-4x128.bin

$A9BA b DameronBack 4 ; The back of Dameron's head (the hair), every form: 4 bytes x 128 lines
> DrawDameronBack $899C, at column (DameronX + $D0) / 8. Read in s5-right.
@res stage5/bitmaps-dameron-back-4x128.bin

$ABBA b DameronFace1 7 ; Dameron's face, form 1: 7 bytes x 128 lines
> DrawDameronFace $8859 in phase 1 (after the first 20 counted hits). Read in rzx-r5 and ending (896 bytes); s5-right counted no hit.
@res stage5/bitmaps-dameron-face1-7x128.bin

$AF3A b DameronFace2 5 ; Dameron's face, form 2: 5 bytes x 128 lines (the skull)
> DrawDameronFace $8859 in phase 2, two columns further right. Read in rzx-r5 and ending (640 bytes).
@res stage5/bitmaps-dameron-face2-5x128.bin

$B1BA b DameronDome3 4 ; The middle of Dameron's head, form 3 (no face): 4 bytes x 128 lines
> DrawDameronDome $894D in phase 3. Read in rzx-r5 and ending (512 bytes).
@res stage5/bitmaps-dameron-dome3-4x128.bin

$B3BA b SpriteBank 3 ; The sprite bank, frames 0-7: 3 bytes x 16 lines (fireballs 0-3, the curved shot 4-7)
> The bank holds 24 frames 3 bytes wide, found through SpriteFrameOffsets $938E: SpriteFrameAddress $9378 gives DE = $B3BA + SpriteFrameOffsets[A]. Frames 0-3 are Dameron's fireball (FireballMissile, PassCounter AND 3), 4-7 the curved shot's (MoveCurvedShot $9DC6 through CurvedShotFrames $9E94). s5-right read frames 0-3 only ($B3BA-$B479); rzx-r5 and ending read all eight.
@res stage5/bitmaps-bank-3x16.bin

$B53A b SpriteBankBolts 3 ; The sprite bank, frames 8-11: 3 bytes x 9 lines, the bolt
> BoltMissile $834E (kind 3, forms 1 and 2). Read in rzx-r5 and ending (all 108 bytes).
@res stage5/bitmaps-bank-3x9.bin

$B5A6 b SpriteBankBursts 3 ; The sprite bank, frames 12-23: 3 bytes x 24 lines, the hero's explosion and the bursts (13 blocks of 72 bytes)
> Frames 12-18 are the hero's explosion and re-forming (DrawHeroFrame $9D85: frame +5 + 12), $13-$17 the bursts round Dameron at a form change (kind 4). Frame 14's offset ($27C) is followed by 144 bytes to frame 15 ($30C): the 72 bytes at SpriteBankSpare $B67E (SpriteBank $B3BA + $2C4) are a frame no offset names, read by no code. rzx-r5 read 360 bytes of the frames, ending 792; the spare frame was read in no recording.
