@module variables
$BA7E b HeroRecord 8 ; The hero's record: +0 X in pixels, +1 the screen line, +4 the state, +5 the frame, +6 the game-over count
> InitHero $7EE9 sets X $40, line $68, state 0, the count $5A; HeroControl $7F1E moves it (X $12-$66, line $40-$96) and steps the explosion; DrawHero $8576 and DrawHeroFrame $9D85 draw it; CheckShotHitsHero $A33E tests the missiles against +0, +1. +2, +3 and +7 are read by no code. The bytes as loaded ($CC $7F $C1 $04 $00 $03 $1F $2B) are overwritten by InitHero before any read. s5-right: 16034 reads of +0/+1, the state 16187.
$BA7F HeroLine ; +1 the screen line
$BA80 HeroUnused2 ; +2, +3: no reader
$BA82 HeroState ; +4: 0 flying, 1 exploding, 2 re-forming, 3 game over
$BA83 HeroFrame ; +5 the explosion's frame
$BA84 HeroGameOverCount ; +6: $5A, - 1 on each even pass in state 3; at 0 MainLoop ends the stage (E = 0)
$BA85 HeroUnused7 ; +7: no reader

$BA86 b Stars 4 ; The 16 stars, 4 bytes each: +0 X in pixels, +1 the screen line, +2 the speed (0 slow, 1 fast), +3 a counter
> InitStars $85F9 seeds them; MoveStars $8627 moves them (4 or 8 pixels a pass to the left) and gives a wrapped star a new line; DrawStars $8672 draws them. The bytes as loaded are overwritten by InitStars. s5-right: 13441 reads.

@module graphics
$BAC6 w UnusedWordTable 8 ; 43 words no code reads: 1, 1000 x 3, 900, 800, 700, 600 x 4, 500 x 2, 400, 300, 200, 100, 60 x 6, 1 x 17, then 0
> A falling table of numbers (a delay or speed schedule) that no stage-5 code uses: no operand names $BAC6-$BB1B and no word in the code area points there (checked over $7800-$A366); no recording (s5-right, rzx-r5, ending) reads any of it. Known only from the bytes.

$BB1C b HeroSprites 3 ; The hero: 12 frames of 3 bytes x 24 lines (3 animation steps x 4 shifts of 2 pixels)
> DrawHero $8576 copies the frame HeroFrames $85D9 names (step (PassCounter AND 7) / 2, step 3 the same as step 1; the shift X AND 6) straight to the screen, no mask. Read in s5-right (1858 reads a byte at most).
@res stage5/bitmaps-hero-3x24.bin

